WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.780
If there's one thing The Walking Dead has
proven over its run, it's that no one is safe.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:09.570
From Lori's disturbing demise to the gruesome
fates of Abraham and Glenn, the AMC series

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:14.099
has made it pretty clear that in Robert Kirkman's
zombie apocalypse, the stakes are high.

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:17.680
One character that has felt untouchable through
all of it has been Rick Grimes.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.000
From the day he woke up in that Georgia hospital,
Rick has beaten the odds quite a bit.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.070
On the heels of Carl's passing, though, it
looks like the show on the verge of an overhaul,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:30.039
and now it's been reported that after season
9, Andrew Lincoln will leave the series that

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:31.259
made him a household name.

00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:34.890
So, how might the end of the Ricktatorship
impact the show moving forward?

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:39.550
Here's what Lincoln's departure probably means
for The Walking Dead.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.870
New leadership

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.540
Viewership for The Walking Dead has been on
a steady decline since the show hit its peak

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.949
in Season 5, and one of the reasons may be
Rick himself.

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:51.640
Over the past few years, we've watched as
Rick repeatedly led the group from one new

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.609
home to another, only to find that the humans
there are more dangerous than zombies.

00:00:55.609 --> 00:00:59.640
Along the way, he's had some very repetitive
struggles with morality that saw him make

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.129
terrible choices, then redeem himself, and
eventually do it all over again.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:08.500
At this point, it's pretty predictable, and
some viewers also think it's a little boring.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.820
Rick's primary motivation to stay in charge
has always been to protect Carl, so now that

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:16.630
he's out of the picture, it's only natural
that the sheriff might finally step aside

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.420
and let someone else take point and that person
might just be Daryl Dixon.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:25.120
AMC may be positioning the crossbow-wielding
motorcycle enthusiast to take over as top

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.120
dog.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.400
Reports say that actor Norman Reedus is negotiating
a sweet new deal with the network that'll

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.810
give him top billing for the series as a whole.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:37.380
Daryl has long been a reliable, capable fan
favorite on the show, and since he never appeared

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.290
in Robert Kirkman's comics, the sky's the
limit as to what he can achieve.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:44.930
Of course, it may be hard to imagine how a
character who's been so quiet and restrained

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:48.950
for all this time can start barking orders
at everybody, but maybe he'll be the kind

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.500
of guy who leads by example instead.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.590
Fractured group

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:57.530
As the bloody battle between Rick and Negan
came to its long-awaited conclusion, a new

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:02.320
conflict emerged: Maggie, Daryl, and
Jesus had formed a secret alliance with the

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.640
end goal of taking down Negan, against Rick's
wishes.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.750
"Rick was wrong to do what he did.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.030
Michonne, too."

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.840
Alexandria and its allies will be dealing
with a fair share of internal conflict in

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.840
the coming episodes, with Negan smiling and
swearing on the sidelines.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.760
What role he'll play during this civil war
remains to be seen, but it may be the catalyst

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.260
to both Rick and Maggie leaving, since Lauren
Cohan is expected to leave the series in the

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.730
coming season as well.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:33.820
With both of the show's de facto leaders on
their way out, and Negan still around causing

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:39.790
everyone problems, we can expect the culmination
of this growing family feud to be pretty spectacular.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.360
Unless…

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.360
New baddies

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:47.290
In the finale's final moments, after showing
leniency to Negan and his Saviors, Rick spoke

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.540
of "a new beginning."

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:52.240
Die-hard comic fans know that means a new
threat is probably on its way.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.860
Next season is expected to begin after a two-year
time jump, and if it's anything like Kirkman's

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:01.319
"A New Beginning" comics arc, we can expect
to meet the Whisperers sooner than later.

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:05.110
Negan's violent acts pushed the envelope for
what can be done on TV, but his brutality

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.360
may be nothing compared to these people.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.800
And their introduction might just give Negan
the opportunity to redeem himself.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.980
If season 9 does end up delivering on the
civil war storyline, it may be possible that

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.650
Negan could prove himself useful.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:20.890
Is it possible that Negan could team up with
Rick, or even Daryl once these Whisperers

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:22.290
make themselves known?

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.930
Stranger things have happened.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:25.930
Lone wolf

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:30.000
Another consequence of the potential "New
Beginning" storyline is that Michonne may

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.590
start going it alone again in the new episodes.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:36.569
In the comics, following the All-Out War with
Negan, Michonne pretty much ran away from

00:03:36.569 --> 00:03:38.220
the group to live out in Oceanside.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.880
While that sounds like more of a Carol move,
it's not out of the question that Michonne

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.200
could separate herself from the rest of the
Alexandria gang if Rick is gone.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.709
After all, when we first met her, the only
company she kept was a pair of jawless walkers.

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:55.090
Rick is the first person she's been romantically
involved with since the trauma of losing her

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.280
boyfriend and son.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:00.040
Their relationship added new layers to the
series, giving them both a welcome sense of

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.190
hope and purpose.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.720
Without Carl to mother, or Rick to comfort,
we might just see Michonne trade in her samurai

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.180
sword for a fishing rod after all.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.349
Rebrand time

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:13.890
After eight seasons, a lot of viewers have
tuned out simply because there's only so much

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.940
misery and grief a person can take from their
entertainment.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:20.560
The network may finally be catching on to
that because losing Carl didn't just spark

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:25.040
the events that transpired in the back half
of season 8, it also set up The Walking Dead

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.780
for a major rebrand effort.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.490
Writer Scott Gimple told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.500
"Story-wise, we knew we were going to be here.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.440
[...] It allows for a new voice to be telling
new stories, and really resets the show in

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.440
a lot of ways."

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:42.050
The voice he's referring to is incoming showrunner
Angela Kang, who'll take over in the new season.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:46.230
Gimple's pivot from showrunner to chief content
officer is not only a change of the guard

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:50.860
behind the camera, it alludes to a new look,
feel, and strategy for the long-running series.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:55.960
"You have to write a character point of view
as if you absolutely believe that to be the

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:56.960
truth."

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:00.800
So, perhaps the new creative direction will
also mean the mood will swing in a direction

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.680
more fans can stomach every week.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:03.680
We'll see.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:04.780
Thanks for watching!

